<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_HuttCartel_EggMarket.xml    ShokkweaveEconomy · WEBWORK_EGG_BLACKMARKET_BUILD_1
  ============================================================================

  §1 of design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/webwork_egg_blackmarket_2026-09-24.md.
  The commission (webwork_owner_and_nest_2026-09-23.md §6 ruling 5): "add the
  black market trader (likely hutt / bounty hunter faction related)". §5
  ruling 1 fronts it as a Hutt Cartel channel — Blackstar (`permanentEnemy
  true`, R12) cannot trade or ask through vanilla machinery, so it appears in
  quest fiction only, never mechanically here.

  Shape copied from the existing `RUT_Caravan_HuttCartel_Captives`
  (UtinniPatches/Defs/TraderKindDefs/RUT_HuttCartel_Captives.xml): a dedicated
  TraderKindDef appended to `RUT_Jawa_HuttCartel`'s own `caravanTraderKinds`
  (see ShokkweaveEggBlackMarket.xml, this mod), never a fixed settlement seat
  (design §1b: "a static buyer next door deletes the [carry-risk] risk").

  🔴 MEASURED, RimSage against the installed 1.6 source (this session,
  2026-09-26) — this is why the design's own §1e "black market BUYS your eggs
  at a premium" row is NOT built here:

    `TraderKindDef.PriceTypeFor(ThingDef, TradeAction)` (Source/RimWorld/
    TraderKindDef.cs) only consults `stockGenerators[i].TryGetPriceType(...)`
    — and therefore only ever returns a non-Normal `PriceType` — when
    `action == TradeAction.PlayerBuys`. For `TradeAction.PlayerSells` (the
    trader buying FROM the player) the method falls straight through to
    `return PriceType.Normal`, unconditionally, for every trader in the game.
    A `StockGenerator`'s `<price>` field (VeryCheap..Exorbitant) is therefore
    LIVE for the sell-to-player side and DEAD for the buy-from-player side —
    no XML lever exists for "this trader pays a premium for tag X". Confirmed
    further: `Settlement_TraderTracker.ColonyThingsWillingToBuy` (and the
    Caravan/TradeShip/Pawn equivalents) hand EVERY carried/caravan item to the
    trade window regardless of the trader's own StockGenerators — a trader
    already accepts a sold egg via ordinary tradeability, it just cannot be
    made to pay MORE for it without a real Harmony patch on
    `TraderKindDef.PriceTypeFor` or `Tradeable.RecalculatePrices`.

    Consequence: the `StockGenerator_BuyTradeTag` below makes this kind WILL
    buy anything tagged `RM_Contraband` (as any Sellable/All trader already
    would), but it prices that purchase at ordinary PriceType.Normal, not the
    design's ❓×1.5 premium. That premium — and the Wildsteam bounty's own
    buy-side premium, `WEBWORK_NEST_EGG_ECONOMY_1`'s scope, same engine limit —
    needs a small Harmony postfix on `TraderKindDef.PriceTypeFor` (or an
    equivalent `Tradeable` price hook) to build for real. Filed as follow-on
    work; nothing here fakes the number.

  The SELL side (black market sells you an egg) has no such limit:
  `PriceType.Expensive` (×2, `PriceTypeUtlity.PriceMultiplier`) DOES apply on
  `TradeAction.PlayerBuys` and lands inside the design's ruled ×1.6-2.0 sell
  premium band (§1e row 1) — the closest of the five discrete PriceType steps
  (VeryCheap .4 / Cheap .7 / Normal 1 / Expensive 2 / Exorbitant 5).

  `commonality` kept low (design §1b: "should feel found, not scheduled" —
  found tuned relative to `RUT_Caravan_HuttCartel_Captives`'s own 0.3, which
  is itself a rare-caravan value; this one halves it, since an egg-selling
  murder-weapon dealer should be rarer than an ordinary debtor-droid fence).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <TraderKindDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.webwork">
    <defName>RUT_Caravan_HuttCartel_EggMarket</defName>
    <label>Hutt Cartel egg broker</label>
    <commonality>0.15</commonality>
    <requestable>false</requestable>
    <orbital>false</orbital>
    <stockGenerators>

      <!-- The black market SELLS you an egg. PriceType.Expensive = x2,
           inside the ruled x1.6-2.0 band (§1e row 1). -->
      <li Class="StockGenerator_SingleDef">
        <thingDef>RM_OllathrixEgg</thingDef>
        <countRange>1~3</countRange>
        <price>Expensive</price>
      </li>

      <!-- The black market BUYS your contraband eggs (and anything else
           tagged RM_Contraband) at ordinary price — see the engine-limit
           note above for why no premium lands here yet. Zero live
           StockGenerator_Tag/_Category anywhere in this repo names
           RM_Contraband (MEASURED: `grep -rn "RM_Contraband" src/` returns
           no hits outside this design's own docs, 2026-09-26), so opening
           the egg's tradeability to All (ShokkweaveEggBlackMarket.xml)
           cannot leak it onto any other trader's shelf by tag route. -->
      <li Class="StockGenerator_BuyTradeTag">
        <tag>RM_Contraband</tag>
      </li>

    </stockGenerators>
  </TraderKindDef>

</Defs>
